(src/duties.vox: the assignment rule; the per-person counts and last-duty
 record.)

a list called 'duty counts' is [].
a list called 'last duty meeting' is [].
a list called 'door holders' is [].
a list called 'auditorium holders' is [].
a list called 'unfilled slots' is [].

To 'prepare the duties'.
  the 'duty counts' is [].
  the 'last duty meeting' is [].
  For each person in names,
    append 0 to 'duty counts',
    append 0 to 'last duty meeting'.
  the 'door holders' is [].
  the 'auditorium holders' is [].
  For each 'meeting number' from 1 to 'meeting count',
    append 0 to 'door holders',
    append 0 to 'auditorium holders'.
  the 'unfilled slots' is [].

To 'a candidate is better than the current best' with a number called candidate and a number called 'the current best'.
  If 'the current best' is 0 then, Return a boolean, true.
  a number called 'the candidate duty count' is element candidate of 'duty counts'.
  a number called 'the current best duty count' is element 'the current best' of 'duty counts'.
  If 'the candidate duty count' is less than 'the current best duty count' then, Return a boolean, true.
  If 'the candidate duty count' is greater than 'the current best duty count' then, Return a boolean, false.
  a number called 'the candidate last duty' is element candidate of 'last duty meeting'.
  a number called 'the current best last duty' is element 'the current best' of 'last duty meeting'.
  Return a boolean, 'the candidate last duty' is less than 'the current best last duty'.

To 'the best person for' with a number called 'meeting number' and a number called 'the person already on duty'.
  a number called 'the best position' is 0.
  For each position from 1 to names's length,
    a text called person is element position of names,
    if position is not 'the person already on duty' and {'is free for meeting' of person and 'meeting number'} and {'a candidate is better than the current best' of position and 'the best position'} then,
      Set 'the best position' to position..
  Return a number, 'the best position'.

To 'record a duty' with a number called position and a number called 'meeting number'.
  a number called 'the new duty count' is {element position of 'duty counts'} add 1.
  Set element position of 'duty counts' to 'the new duty count'.
  Set element position of 'last duty meeting' to 'meeting number'.

To 'assign the duties of meeting' with a number called 'meeting number'.
  a text called 'the meeting label' is 'the label of meeting' of 'meeting number'.
  a number called 'the door holder' is 'the best person for' of 'meeting number' and 0.
  Set element 'meeting number' of 'door holders' to 'the door holder'.
  If 'the door holder' is 0 then,
    append "{'the meeting label'} door: nobody is available" to 'unfilled slots'.
  Otherwise,
    'record a duty' of 'the door holder' and 'meeting number'.
  a number called 'the auditorium holder' is 'the best person for' of 'meeting number' and 'the door holder'.
  Set element 'meeting number' of 'auditorium holders' to 'the auditorium holder'.
  If 'the auditorium holder' is 0 then,
    append "{'the meeting label'} auditorium: nobody is available" to 'unfilled slots'.
  Otherwise,
    'record a duty' of 'the auditorium holder' and 'meeting number'.

To 'assign every duty'.
  For each 'meeting number' from 1 to 'meeting count', 'assign the duties of meeting' of 'meeting number'.
